31,2,1,talk,Midori,,I found that joint clinics often fail due to rota disputes. We need a stable structure.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Interestingly, a previous call-back trial significantly reduced readmissions for the elderly. It worked.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"We have severe nursing vacancies, but the midwifery rota actually has some unusual slack.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The budget is down by a quarter, and off-site contacts bring in zero tariff revenue.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,The car park is full by eleven and rooms are booked out. We have no space.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, if off-site work earns nothing, we must be very cautious about home-visit models.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"But @Shion, the readmission data proves those contacts save the hospital money in the long run.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Misaki,,We can't add pressure to ward nurses. Any new program must use existing slack.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, long-term savings don't fix a current budget deficit and a lack of immediate tariffs.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"Exactly. And if it's on-site, we have no rooms. If it's off-site, we have no money.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Misaki, if midwifery has slack, perhaps a program centered there would be more sustainable.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,We should prioritize the patient outcome. The readmission drop was a fifth; that is significant.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Misaki,,I agree with Midori. Using the midwifery slack avoids burning out the ward staff.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Shion,,Any plan requiring outside surgery data agreements will also be a nightmare; they take forever.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,We must avoid anything that adds more cars to the lot or more slots to the system.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Midori,,It seems we need something that uses available staff and doesn't require new infrastructure.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,As long as it provides a measurable benefit to the patients.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Misaki,,Midwifery is the only area where we aren't already drowning.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Shion,,And it must be on-site to ensure we can actually bill for the sessions.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"If it fits the current rota and doesn't overflow the rooms, I can support it.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
