56,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Looking at the candidates, the Perinatal Support Service seems the safest for stability.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The Home Follow-Up Team matches the successful trial data, but the funding is a risk.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Home Follow-Up would crush the ward nurses. Perinatal uses the midwifery slack.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Shion,,Chronic Care Coordination requires outside data agreements and off-site work. It is logically unsound.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,The Day Rehab Unit would require too much space and parking. It's impossible.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, the Home Follow-Up Team also risks the same failure as the shared nursing rounds.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,That is true. The shared rounds had high failure rates due to access issues.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Misaki,,Perinatal Support is the only one that aligns with our staffing reality.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Shion,,"Perinatal is on-site, meaning we get the tariffs. It's the only financially viable option.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,It also doesn't seem to require the same volume of bookings as a full rehab unit.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Midori,,I'm convinced. Perinatal Support avoids the inter-departmental rota wars we've seen before.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"If the other options are physically or financially impossible, I will concede to Perinatal.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Misaki,,It's the most responsible choice for the staff.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Shion,,It is the only choice that doesn't bankrupt the development fund in year two.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I agree. It is the most absorbable program.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Midori,,Let us vote.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Misaki,,Ready.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Shion,,Let's proceed.,"{""words"":2,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,Ready.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
